cript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-03-18T08:40:03Z","updated_at":"2025-03-18T14:52:23Z","closed_at":"2025-03-18T14:47:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproductible in Godot 4.3 stable\n- Reproductible in Godot 4.4 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI created a script in which i've written an export_enum(), with two values. If I change the value name in the script, it does not update in the inspector, even if I reload the scene. I must manually re-select the value in the inspector, which is quite a bit annoying.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c81b325e-1360-4beb-a518-460c7208bc3a\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5945c6df-2885-44ff-81a1-a67bf64567bb\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a blank script\n- Write for instance ```@export_enum(\"Type1\", \"Type4\") var enum_type = \"Type1\"```\n- Select a value in the inspector\n- Change the selected value name in code and save\n- You should notice that the value name does not update in the inspector\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp-enum_4.4.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19313996/mrp-enum_4.4.zip)\n\n[mrp-enum_4.3.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19313436/mrp-enum_4.3.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"SilverWolveGames","id":92260598,"node_id":"U_kgDOBX_I9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuser